markScheme:
4 marks for 4 of:
Attributions - perceived reasons for performance/outcome;
Failure to internal-unstable factors/effort (Weiner's Model on its own gains no marks - must be reference to applied use);
Failure to external-unstable factors/luck;
Failure to external-stable factors/task difficulty;
Failure to external control, eg those areas which the player cannot influence;
Not internal-stable factors, eg ability (accept reverse answer);
(Not learned helplessness/self-efficacy)
Self-serving bias;
Attribution re-training.
(Don't just accept 'external factors' or 'internal factors'.)
Max 4 marks.
